**Common Hanging Patterns**

```java
// Pattern 1: Classic Deadlock
public class OrderService {
  private final Object lock1 = new Object();
  private final Object lock2 = new Object();

  public void method1() {
    synchronized (lock1) {
      // Do work
      synchronized (lock2) { // Acquires lock1 then lock2
        // Do more work
      }
    }
  }

  public void method2() {
    synchronized (lock2) {
      // Do work
      synchronized (lock1) { // Acquires lock2 then lock1 = DEADLOCK!
        // Do more work
      }
    }
  }
}

// Fix: Always acquire locks in same order
public class OrderService {
  public void method1() {
    synchronized (lock1) {
      synchronized (lock2) { // Always lock1 → lock2
        // Work
      }
    }
  }

  public void method2() {
    synchronized (lock1) {
      synchronized (lock2) { // Same order
        // Work
      }
    }
  }
}

// Pattern 2: Database Connection Pool Exhausted
public class OrderService {
  public void processOrder(Order order) {
    Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection(); // Blocks if pool empty!
    // Long-running query
    // If all threads blocked here = app hangs
  }
}

// Thread dump shows:
"http-nio-8080-exec-1" waiting for monitor entry
  at com.zaxxer.hikari.pool.HikariPool.getConnection(HikariPool.java:197)
  - waiting to lock <0x00000000d5e2c088> (a com.zaxxer.hikari.pool.HikariPool)

// Fix: Use try-with-resources, increase pool size, fix slow queries
public class OrderService {
  public void processOrder(Order order) {
    try (Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection()) {
      // Use connection
    } // Auto-closed
  }
}

// Pattern 3: Blocked on External Call
public class PaymentService {
  public PaymentResult charge(Order order) {
    // Synchronous HTTP call to payment gateway
    ResponseEntity<PaymentResult> response = restTemplate.postForEntity(
      "https://payment-gateway.com/charge",
      request,
      PaymentResult.class
    ); // If gateway slow/down, thread blocks indefinitely

    return response.getBody();
  }
}

// Thread dump shows:
"http-nio-8080-exec-5" runnable
  at java.net.SocketInputStream.socketRead0(Native Method)
  at java.net.SocketInputStream.read(SocketInputStream.java:150)
  at sun.security.ssl.InputRecord.readFully(InputRecord.java:465)
  ...
  at org.springframework.web.client.RestTemplate.postForEntity(RestTemplate.java:589)

// Fix: Set timeouts
@Bean
public RestTemplate restTemplate() {
  HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory factory = 
    new HttpComponentsClientHttpRequestFactory();
  factory.setConnectTimeout(5000);      // 5s connect timeout
  factory.setReadTimeout(10000);        // 10s read timeout

  return new RestTemplate(factory);
}

// Better: Use Circuit Breaker
@CircuitBreaker(name = "paymentService", fallbackMethod = "chargeFallback")
public PaymentResult charge(Order order) {
  return paymentGateway.charge(order);
}

// Pattern 4: Infinite Loop
public class DataProcessor {
  public void processData(List<Data> data) {
    while (true) { // Infinite loop!
      // Process
      if (someCondition) {
        break; // But condition never true
      }
    }
  }
}

// Thread dump shows same stack trace across multiple dumps:
"data-processor-thread" runnable
  at com.example.DataProcessor.processData(DataProcessor.java:45)
  at com.example.DataProcessor.processData(DataProcessor.java:45)
  at com.example.DataProcessor.processData(DataProcessor.java:45)
  # Same line number = stuck in loop

// Fix: Add timeout or iteration limit
public class DataProcessor {
  public void processData(List<Data> data) {
    int maxIterations = 1000;
    int count = 0;

    while (count < maxIterations) {
      // Process
      if (someCondition) {
        break;
      }
      count++;
    }

    if (count >= maxIterations) {
      log.error("Exceeded max iterations, possible infinite loop");
    }
  }
}
```

**Step 4: Immediate Mitigation**

```bash
# Option 1: Restart application (fastest)
kubectl rollout restart deployment/order-service

# Option 2: Kill specific thread (risky)
jstack <pid> | grep "Thread-Name"
# Note thread ID (nid=0x1234)
kill -9 <thread-id>
# May cause unpredictable behavior

# Option 3: Scale up (if connection pool issue)
kubectl scale deployment/order-service --replicas=10

# Option 4: Enable emergency bypass
# If payment gateway down, switch to queue-based processing
```

**Step 5: Prevent Hangs**

```java
// 1. Always set timeouts
@Bean
public RestTemplate restTemplate() {
  SimpleClientHttpRequestFactory factory = new SimpleClientHttpRequestFactory();
  factory.setConnectTimeout(5000);
  factory.setReadTimeout(10000);
  return new RestTemplate(factory);
}

// 2. Use timeouts for blocking operations
public class OrderService {
  private final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();

  public Order getOrder(String id) throws TimeoutException {
    Future<Order> future = executor.submit(() -> orderRepository.findById(id));

    try {
      return future.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS); // 5s timeout
    } catch (TimeoutException e) {
      future.cancel(true);
      throw new TimeoutException("Order lookup timed out");
    }
  }
}

// 3. Avoid nested synchronized blocks
// Use java.util.concurrent locks instead
private final Lock lock1 = new ReentrantLock();
private final Lock lock2 = new ReentrantLock();

public void method1() {
  if (lock1.tryLock(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
    try {
      if (lock2.tryLock(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
        try {
          // Do work
        } finally {
          lock2.unlock();
        }
      }
    } finally {
      lock1.unlock();
    }
  }
}

// 4. Monitor thread states
@Component
public class ThreadMonitor {
  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 30000)
  public void monitorThreads() {
    ThreadMXBean threadBean = ManagementFactory.getThreadMXBean();
    long[] deadlockedThreads = threadBean.findDeadlockedThreads();

    if (deadlockedThreads != null) {
      log.error("DEADLOCK DETECTED! {} threads deadlocked", 
        deadlockedThreads.length);
      // Alert, capture thread dump
    }

    // Check for blocked threads
    ThreadInfo[] threads = threadBean.dumpAllThreads(true, true);
    long blockedCount = Arrays.stream(threads)
      .filter(t -> t.getThreadState() == Thread.State.BLOCKED)
      .count();

    if (blockedCount > 10) {
      log.warn("{} threads currently blocked", blockedCount);
    }
  }
}
```

Key steps: Confirm hang → Thread dump → Analyze patterns → Mitigate → Prevent recurrence.
